-- Node: wct-end (3 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"info","module":6,"title":"WCT Management Complete","body":"**Key Takeaways:**\n\n1. **80% of WCT is VT** — treat as VT when in doubt\n2. **Stability does NOT differentiate** VT from SVT\n3. **Procainamide > amiodarone** for stable VT (PROCAMIO)\n4. 🛑 **Before procainamide, rule out sodium channel blockade** — procainamide is itself a sodium channel blocker. Wide out of proportion to the rate, wide *and* slow, an aVR terminal R ≥3 mm, or any exposure history means **bicarbonate, not procainamide**\n5. **Wide and slow after an overdose is pre-terminal**, not a rhythm that is settling down\n6. **Torsades: magnesium** — NOT amiodarone\n7. **Irregular WCT: avoid AV nodal blockers** (may be WPW)\n8. **Admit all VT** — EP consult for ICD evaluation\n\n[WCT Stop Page](#/info/wide-complex-tachycardia-stop)","citation":[1,5,8,16],"summary":"WCT complete. 80% is VT. Rule out sodium channel blockade before procainamide. Torsades = Mg. Irregular WCT = no AV nodal blockers. Admit all."}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'wct-end' AND tree_id = 'wide-complex-tachycardia';

-- Node: wct-doubt (4 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"info","module":5,"title":"When In Doubt — Treat as VT","body":"**The safe approach when diagnosis is uncertain:**\n\n✅ **VT treatments are SAFE for SVT:**\n• Procainamide will not harm SVT patient\n• Cardioversion will not harm SVT patient\n• Amiodarone will not harm SVT patient\n\n❌ **SVT treatments may KILL VT patient:**\n• Adenosine: usually ineffective, may degenerate to VF\n• Verapamil/Diltiazem: negative inotropy + vasodilation = collapse\n• Beta-blockers: similar risk\n\n**Bottom line:**\n**If ANY doubt → procainamide or cardioversion**\n\n---\n\n🛑 **The one exception to \"procainamide is safe.\"** This rule holds when the choice is between ventricular tachycardia and supraventricular tachycardia with aberrancy. It does **not** hold if the wide QRS is caused by a drug blocking the sodium channel — a tricyclic antidepressant, cocaine, diphenhydramine, flecainide, or any of the other agents in that class. Procainamide is itself a sodium channel blocker, and in a poisoned patient it stacks a second blockade onto a failing conduction system.\n\n**Cardioversion, by contrast, is safe in every one of these scenarios.** If you are unstable and unsure, use electricity.","citation":[1,2,5,16],"next":"wct-procainamide-gate","summary":"When in doubt = VT. VT treatments safe for SVT — EXCEPT procainamide in sodium channel blocker poisoning. Cardioversion is always safe.","safetyLevel":"critical"}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'wct-doubt' AND tree_id = 'wide-complex-tachycardia';

